{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991057-2e-orders-obsessions","id":991057,"title":"[2E] Orders' Obsessions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-21T12:08:25-07:00","id":991057,"title":"[2E] Orders' Obsessions","content":"Opening sum up of idea - <b>Characters can take more broad interpretations of their Orders Mysteries as his more broader Obsession.</b><br /> <br /> * <b>Adamantine Arrows</b> - <i>Oaths</i> - Examples are classical 'Protect my cabal'<br /> * <b>Free Council</b> - <i>Techne</i> - Examples are various Sleepers occult traditions or technical disciplines Also, parts of Libertine Creed - one players choose for our game 'Servants of Lie' as his Obsession. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> * <b>Guardians of Veil </b>- <i>Persons and Beings</i> - Abyssal Intruders and Hieromagus are examples, particular Sleeper in Labyrinth would be other.<br /> * <b>Mysterium</b> - <i>Disciplines of Order</i> - I.E.<ul><li>Magosophy</li> <li>Supernology</li> <li>Thaumatology</li> <li>Occultism</li> <li>Sidereology</li> <li>Teratology</li> <li>Exoterics ( Each one of Sleepers arts and humanities )</li> </ul>* <b>Silver Ladder </b>- <i>Persons and Institutions</i> - Elemental Pilgrimage and Lion-Sage-Stag are particulars in here, promising Sleeper student would be other. Looking over church, company or government office.<br /> * <b>Seers of Throne</b> - Signs of Exarchs - Mystery Commands are particulars here.<br /> <br /> <i>Rest of opening idea that sprung this take on Obsessions:</i><br /> One of my players have very cool idea for Mysterium characters - instead of normal Obsessions of rest mages being particular and defined Mysteries - Mystygoges can choose one of thier disxiplines of Knowledge. It lead to interesting characters as Mysterium members devoted not only to particular supenatural being or realm, but rather whole category. Like mage can be Obsessed over werewolves or vampires. Mysterium members can be over all supernatural races. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-30-2017, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T12:34:31-07:00","id":991063,"title":"","content":"Doesn't seem like it actually adds anything to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T12:37:45-07:00","id":991065,"title":"","content":"That's actually how I think about my Mysterium members, albeit without thinking in terms of Obsession. I use the categories of research given in the Mysterium book, who's into what, and then pick one little thing that makes them experts in the field. Like I've got a Supernologist Acanthus (Dudekos Superior) who has perform especial study in Ananke. Useful if I ever decide to drop one in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T12:42:32-07:00","id":991066,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but Wyrd doesn't seem to be talking about having Mysterium members interested in super specific Mysteries like that, but in blowing it up into broader categories of interest. Which frankly, isn't any different than what regular Mages can do anyway, ST permitting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T12:43:05-07:00","id":991067,"title":"","content":"I don't see how or why it'd be particularly different. &quot;I want to know more about werewolves&quot; is functionally indistinguishable from &quot;Observe werewolves on a sacred hunt&quot; because the latter is how the former manifests in an A-Beat-worthy manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T13:11:38-07:00","id":991079,"title":"","content":"Wyrd is apparently making the distinction that regular Mages can choose to study werewolves, or vampires, but Mysterium should be able to study both simultaneously as one Obsession. That's how I read it anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T13:12:39-07:00","id":991080,"title":"","content":"I mean that Mysterium's members could take Obsessions as those broad categories from Disciplines in Order:<ul><li>Magosophy</li> <li>Supernology</li> <li>Thaumatology</li> <li>Occultism</li> <li>Sidereology</li> <li>Teratology</li> <li>Exoterics ( Each one of Sleepers arts and humanities )</li> </ul>Each member can declare any of those as his Obsession and work with their definition. For example, Teratology will gives Arcane Beats on any supernatural monster examined, not only limited to particulars like 'vampires' or 'werewolves'. Probably would limit this 'Master Thesis' Obsession to only one slot per character, as it's specially much broader.<br /> <br /> More thinking about this idea, I come to believe other Orders also have similar 'Special Order's Obsessions' - Arrows can take on Obsessions their Oaths, Free Council can dwell in to their Techne culture as source of Supernal Knowledge, and Seers of Throne can have Mystery Commands from Exarchs. Interesting would be thinking about ideas for Silver Ladder and Guardians of the Veil - maybe Silver Ladder of Being for first one and something about <i>destroying </i>Mysteries?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T13:24:03-07:00","id":991084,"title":"","content":"It's still not anything new.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the Guardians would obviously Obsess over their Masques and the Heiromagus. The Silver Ladder would be looking into the elemental precepts and explore the depths of the Lion, Stag and Sage.<br /> <br /> Technically, any faction in an Order could be Obsessed with whatever that faction is about. For instance the Power Brokers in the Silver Ladder could be obsessed with Power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T22:30:24-07:00","id":991285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991057-2e-orders-obsessions?p=991084#post991084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, the Guardians would obviously Obsess over their Masques and the Heiromagus.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how would those works in play? Hieromagus plot I run myself, but Masques do not sound as something you dwell in to longer than 'I take my Masque number...'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991057-2e-orders-obsessions?p=991084#post991084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Silver Ladder would be looking into the elemental precepts and explore the depths of the Lion, Stag and Sage.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I totally do not see on session-to-session basis. How those Obsession could work? Much more probable are Silver Ladder of Being in my POV.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T05:33:46-07:00","id":991351,"title":"","content":"They're mystery religions, their precepts are built on mysteries. It's too bad you can't figure out how to use that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T07:46:39-07:00","id":991393,"title":"","content":"I ask juat for story seeds/actions beside 'I take Masque number X'. For Mysterium you just put PC against types of Discipline that he is aimed at. Arrow juat fullfil his word made under Oath. Libertines study occult symbols of Techne and casting by it. What Guardians or Ladder mages do to get Arcane Beats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T09:54:46-07:00","id":991421,"title":"","content":"I told you, and you didn't understand how it could work. It's not just, &quot;I take Masque X&quot; it's, &quot;What is Masque X like? How does it manifest? How is it different then me? Where's my true self if I'm always in my Masque?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Masques, the Heiromagus, the Elemental Precepts, the Lion, Stag and Sage are all valid Mysteries, it's just a matter of framing the question. If you don't know how to do that, eh. You don't really need to, there are plenty of other things to be Obsessed about.<br /> <br /> My main point from the beginning is that the broad categories of study that the Mysterium engage in isn't really an innovative use of Obsession, because anything that you don't fully understand can be one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T10:41:59-07:00","id":991442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991057-2e-orders-obsessions?p=991285#post991285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how would those works in play?</div> </div> </div> </div>To answer this question is something that has to be at least <i>modestly</i> taken care of on an individual basis. Different Mages will pursue different Mysteries in different ways.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, if you wanted to include a system like this, what I <i>wouldn't</i> do is just let a character take &quot;Teratology&quot; or what have you as a Mystery, but ask your players to list on their sheets somewhere a small constellation of broad Mysteries that the character easily obsesses over. Werewolves, Sleepwalkers, &quot;Magic Is Alive&quot;, Masques, etc. Then just use the existing rule that, at any time, a character can switch out an Aspiration/Obsession to one more relevant to the story if appropriate.<br /> <br /> In the case of Guardian Masques, &quot;Acquire Mask X&quot; is probably kinda dull on its face if the character is literally just spending XP to get it. That's not an Obsession because it doesn't actually change the gameplay; it is just twisting mechanics for an XP discount (and a minor one at that). If a character lists that masque as an Obsession, the only smart thing to do is to <i>not</i> let them buy it. At least, not straight away.<br /> <br /> Instead, provide the character with a teacher. This doesn't need to be a <i>person</i>, but it does need to be a related opportunity; something that requires them to immerse themselves in the character or nature of the Masque in such a way that puts them in some sort of danger. This need not be violent; it could be social or mystical danger.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, let's say you've got Lucifer, a Mastigos Guardian who wants to acquire the Adversary Masque. Lucifer wants the mask because it lets him engage in subterfuge and deception without guilt (or with less guilt, at least); adopting a persona whose nature is to oppose, subvert, and ruin. Developing an insight into a mystical personality is <i>hard</i>, though; you can't just go &quot;Oh, okay, I'm gonna be a professional bastard today&quot;. This is serious mental programming and mystical union. It requires serious difficulty and effort.<br /> <br /> So Lucifer spends his days reading history books on famous betrayals; psychology texts about all the human safeguards against betrayal buried in our evolutionary past; forces himself to commit small betrayals like short-changing stores (something for which his Wisdom might suffer).<br /> <br /> The whole thing comes to a head when Lucifer has a vision of his own conscience standing watch over his psyche; <i>pleading</i> with him to turn back from this path; to refuse to engage in this behaviour. When he refuses, it transforms into a great flaming angel and declares that so long as it lives, his conscience shall never be clean. So long as his conscience is not clean and pure - so long as his mind is not absolutely dedicated to the effort - he shall never become the Adversary.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'll give you an A-Beat if Lucifer flatly ignores this and goes diving in his Oneiros to defeat his conscience,&quot; the ST says.<br /> <br /> So Lucifer does what any sane and sensible person does and goes to fight his conscience in the Astral. An adventure is had in which he and any other players go traveling through his inner world and he is forced to reveal parts of himself to them that maybe he didn't want to show off.<br /> <br /> (Don't make it too overt but, yeah, this is his own mind betraying him to his closest friends; how more intimate a betrayal can you get?)<br /> <br /> Until at last, he finds his conscience, which pleads with him to not go any further.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'll offer you an A-Beat if you refuse,&quot; says the ST.<br /> <br /> So Lucifer goes on to beat his conscience into submission before all and sundry; bending and breaking its will with spells and magic; grinding his Wisdom against a rough stone with every casting until the bright angel is broken, its pure body split with wounds, its blazing wings cut to bloody stumps, and its sublime face made to shed bitter tears as Lucifer binds it in chains and makes it submit before his indomitable will.<br /> <br /> Lucifer's Path is now clear (yes, that's deliberate capitalization). He has been betrayed by his own soul and betrayed it in turn. Nothing within himself can conquer his highest drives; his self-determination; his self-realization; his self. His ego.<br /> <br /> There, at the entrance of a tainted and corrupted garden, Lucifer finds a snake's skin and slips it over his body, and becomes, at last, the Adversary.<br /> <br /> &quot;Alright,&quot; says the ST, &quot;you can buy the merit now.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's how you make an Order-focused Obsession interesting. Not just &quot;Okay, buy it off your sheet&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T18:23:05-07:00","id":991644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991057-2e-orders-obsessions?p=991442#post991442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's how you make an Order-focused Obsession interesting. Not just &quot;Okay, buy it off your sheet&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this <i>is</i> a problem. Mysterium player just write his Obsessions as 'Monsters/places/Astral' and it's totally valid Obsession from Order's perspective - and ST just need to add those elements in play as background of plot. Free Council guy just try to experiment on his magic with his newest pop culture fix and call it Techne. Adamantine Arrow just says 'I will protect you' or 'We will take revenge', do this and it's more than enough to fulfill his Obsessions.<br /> <br /> From yours POV Guardians need to take his cabal mates on vision quest to show them his most sacred places, betray his own psych twice, and return to reality just with two new A Beats - where rest Orders just easily can get those in totally normal two scenes not needing any of this ( well, most of time ). Guardian to buy his new Merit <i>cannot</i> ( in reality ) repeat in using to get more A Beats from it - where rest of Orders just lunch on anything easily provided to their ethos. Not too mention that you <i>do not </i>buy your Merits from Arcane Beats.<br /> <br /> Masques scenario as Obsessions is unreal from two more reasons:<br /> 1. Guardians are all about security and secrecy. They <i>do not</i> share their Oneiros stuff with other cabalmates if they do not need it. It's both positive to both sides, as imagining Oneiros of long term Guardian, it would be just one big trauma to everyone.<br /> 2. Guardians <i>aren't</i> really about Masques in core of their tenets. They are about protecting - and sometimes destroying - Mysteries. It's contrasted with other Orders as Mysterium are <i>really</i> about uncovering various lore, Arrows are <i>really</i> about servitude and challenges and Free Council is <i>really</i> about 'human-made' magic. That FC's Merit is also their main dogma is just coincidence. Mysterium's Egregore Merit is other thing from their Obsessions. Arrows Adamantine Hand is other thing from their Obsessions. Ladders Lex Magica Merit is surely other thing from their Obsessions.<br /> <br /> Can Guardian choose Masque as his Obsession? Sure, but it's the same way as Mysterium can choose Egregore or Arrow can choose Adamantine Hand - they will get one or maybe two A Beats from exploring this before buying Merit - and that's it. On the other hand, Mysterium and Arrows will have whole new <b>category</b> of Obsessions still to explore on each and every session. I do not see this with Guardians and would want them to have something like this. ( Silver Ladder also, for that matter. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-22-2016, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T18:44:39-07:00","id":991647,"title":"","content":"Proposal - <b>What if Guardians thing is being Obsessed over <i>other people</i> ( Sleepers, mages or supernaturals )?</b> They are known from stalking moves of every other sorcerers, in the end. it also nicely joins with their running Sleepers inside Labyrinth and watching over newly Awakened. It also nicely ties in with Order's Hieromagus Obsession and, from perspective, to Masques! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Or maybe that Guardians can take as their Obsessions the <i>Obsessions of others</i>?</b> Like, Awakened is Obsessed over book - and by this, Guardian is Obsessed with book now to get to it first?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-22-2016, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T20:33:01-07:00","id":991688,"title":"","content":"No, it's basically that you don't get it. I hate the say that, but you just...don't get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T00:27:55-07:00","id":991762,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if that's what you got from what I said, I don't know what to tell you, Wyrd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T00:45:54-07:00","id":991765,"title":"","content":"I UNDERSTAND that Obsessions are individual for every mage. BUT Order can give you more broad interpretaion ( like Mysterium ) or totally non-supernatural ( like Arrows ). As Obsessoons give Arcane Beats, it means that Mysterium, Arrow and Free Council have easier time to get theirs. I just want to even scales for Guardians and Ladder. Watching over person, testing her in Veils and watching over Labirynth sounds as good for GotV. It also ties to Hieromagus and Masques in interpretation as 'Obsessions on Persons'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T04:27:36-07:00","id":991800,"title":"","content":"More thinking about sum up of Orders Obsessions:<br /> * <b>Adamantine Arrows</b> - Oaths<br /> * <b>Free Council</b> - Techne<br /> * <b>Guardians of Veil </b>- Persons and beings - Abyssal Intruders and Hieromagus are particular examples<br /> * <b>Mysterium</b> - Disciplines of Order<br /> * <b>Silver Ladder </b>- Persons and institutions - Elemental Pilgrimage and Lion-Sage-Stag are particulars in here<br /> * <b>Seers of Throne</b> - Signs of Exarchs - Mystery Commands are particulars here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-31-2016, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T06:07:43-07:00","id":991814,"title":"","content":"Umm.... can I ask a question? How is this different than the Mysteries blurb in each Order write up? I feel like you're just repeating what's already written down, so all you need to do is just make it give bonuses ala Obsession rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T07:45:13-07:00","id":991848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991057-2e-orders-obsessions?p=991814#post991814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is this different than the Mysteries blurb in each Order write up?</div> </div> </div> </div>In reality - it's not very different than Orders blurbs. I just want to make them more clear for players. We got those positives of my idea:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Arcane Beats from mundane actions</b> - In 2E <b>Mage</b> corebook there is: <i>'Obsessions are just like long-term Aspirations, except they relate specifically to a mage\u2019s compulsion to explore the mystical in her life. They could be goals to learn or research specific things. They could be player goals for the character to encounter certain strangeness in the world. They could be goals to use magic in new or extreme ways. '</i> - It's all sounds as Obsessions are <b>only</b> about uncovering Mysteries with or from magic, <i>not</i> that they could be about 'mundane' actions. Arrow swors Oath and can change it into Obsession. Mysterium member choose his Discipline to be Exoterics ( Litrature ) and get's Arcane Beats just by looking for very rare English books. Guardian stalks some Sleeper, trying to judge if he will make good Awakened, without any hint of supernatural sings. All those, by normal rules, would not give you Arcane Beats. But letting them took as Obsessions open this to playing your Order dogma in 'non-magical way', and still get Arcane Experience. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2. <b>We got 'typical' Obsessions for Orders</b> - I also run game for new, young players. They read their 2E corebook Orders sections, but still do not grasp what 'typical Guardian' is Obsessed with. ( Beside Heiromagus that is cool idea - I use it as premise of other game - but rather niche one ). Pointing to 'You can stalk people to check them if they will be good Awakened or menace' just solves those kind of thing. For Silver Ladder, I must admit, I did not have any idea for good Obsessions before I started this topic. And I have 12+ years of experience with <b>Mage</b> - what are to say fresh players. Pointing to 'typical Order's Obsessions' is good here. It also nicely rounds for NPC character - if you do not have ideas for non-personal mage's Obsessions, just choose one from his Orders. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 3. <b>They are much shorter sum-ups than Orders blurbs.</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T23:54:10-08:00","id":1040462,"title":"","content":"Latest iteration of idea:<br /> <br /> Opening sum up of idea - <b>Characters can take more broad interpretations of their Orders Mysteries as his more broader Obsession.</b><br /> <br /> * <b>Adamantine Arrows</b> - <i>Oaths</i> - Examples are classical 'Protect my cabal'<br /> * <b>Free Council</b> - <i>Techne</i> - Examples are various Sleepers occult traditions or technical disciplines Also, parts of Libertine Creed - one players choose for our game 'Servants of Lie' as his Obsession. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<br /> * <b>Guardians of Veil </b>- <i>Persons and Beings</i> - Abyssal Intruders and Hieromagus are examples, particular Sleeper in Labyrinth would be other.<br /> * <b>Mysterium</b> - <i>Disciplines of Order</i> - I.E.<ul><li>Magosophy</li> <li>Supernology</li> <li>Thaumatology</li> <li>Occultism</li> <li>Sidereology</li> <li>Teratology</li> <li>Exoterics ( Each one of Sleepers arts and humanities )</li> </ul>* <b>Silver Ladder </b>- <i>Persons and Institutions</i> - Elemental Pilgrimage and Lion-Sage-Stag are particulars in here, promising Sleeper student would be other. Looking over church, company or government office.<br /> * <b>Seers of Throne</b> - Signs of Exarchs - Mystery Commands are particulars here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}